[ceiling] Functional flat shell-bearing flange: this print-down Z46.1 face is the underside of the drop-in roof surround. Its horizontal surface seats on the four shell-rooted ledges while the upward screws clamp the frame. The frame prints on its lower feet; this flange therefore uses accessible Tree(auto)/Default supports under the documented enclosure support-removal strategy. Current support placement, release effort and finished fit remain scoped to a fresh slice/print.
alternatives: Sloping the seating face removes the shared horizontal shell bearing or changes its mating ledges. Filling down to the bed closes the required under-funnel connection space. Retain the named bearing plane and its supported manufacturing treatment.
