[thin] Finite M3 head seats and their through-hole surrounds: the rear raised Ø5.5 mm head-bearing pads have a 1.1 mm radial annulus outside the Ø3.3 mm shank clearance. The four screw seats retain the complete annulus through the full 5.8 mm grip, as measured in drop-in-review/plain-stock-review.json. The front 1.6 mm and rear 1.9 mm picks are the local shank-to-edge sections of these same fastener seats at Z47.1–50.9, rather than a separate enclosure wall. This answer is limited to the four specified M3 seats; clamp force and printed durability remain unqualified.
alternatives: Filling a shank bore prevents fitting the selected M3 screw. Removing its surrounding seat removes head bearing. Increasing the surround into the silicone pocket changes the selected brim clearance, while shifting screw axes changes the matching full-wall shell insert hosts. Keep the finite, fully measured head-seat annuli and their fixed screw axes.
